==English==

===Etymology 1===
Confer Middle English {{term|faden||to flatter|lang=enm}}, and Old English {{term|fgan||to join, unite|lang=ang}}, German {{term|fügen|lang=de}}, or Old English {{term|afægian|āfægian|to depict|lang=ang}}; all perhaps form the same root as the English {{term|fair}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|fadg|ing}}

# {{context|obscure|transitive}} To fit or suit.
# {{context|obscure|transitive}} To [[agree]].
# {{context|obscure|transitive}} To [[succeed]].
# {{Geordie}} To [[eat]] together.
A VAGINA

===Etymology 2===
Etymology uncertain

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|Ulster}} Irish [[potato bread]] - flat [[farl]]s, griddle-baked. Often served fried.
# {{New Zealand}} A wool pack. traditionally made of jute now often synthetic.
# {{Geordie}} Small bread loaf or bun made with left-over dough.

